1
00:00:50,971 --> 00:00:52,768
I'm throwing you, okay?

2
00:01:08,591 --> 00:01:10,614
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

3
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:14,314
I did it, right?

4
00:01:15,544 --> 00:01:17,161
Right?

5
00:01:22,336 --> 00:01:24,570
Oh my Gosh!

6
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:26,598
<i>What is this?</i>

7
00:01:32,523 --> 00:01:34,278
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

8
00:01:35,236 --> 00:01:36,784
Get up.

9
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:39,259
Hurry, get up.

10
00:01:46,611 --> 00:01:48,444
<i>Yoon Ha Na?</i>

11
00:01:57,654 --> 00:01:59,588
<i>Let's do it one more time.</i>

12
00:02:11,806 --> 00:02:17,049
Why did they call Dangun Wanggeom of Gojoseon
the king of theocracy?

13
00:02:18,484 --> 00:02:20,994
Hey, what's with the attitude?

14
00:02:22,547 --> 00:02:24,544
He didn't only have a hand in politics,

15
00:02:24,544 --> 00:02:26,644
- but took part in rituals...
<i>- When we go back,</i>

16
00:02:26,644 --> 00:02:28,766
<i>we get Woo Jae back into sports.</i>

17
00:02:28,766 --> 00:02:30,464
<i>What will you do?</i>

18
00:02:30,464 --> 00:02:33,161
<i>I'll be the one in your body, not you.</i>

19
00:02:33,161 --> 00:02:34,574
<i>Don't worry about it.</i>

20
00:02:34,574 --> 00:02:36,170
<i>Yoon Ha Ru's body?</i>

21
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:39,591
<i>It's already been perfected by senior year.</i>

22
00:02:40,868 --> 00:02:43,290
- In the roots of our history...
- I wonder if Yoon Ha Na is doing okay?

23
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:45,594
there were communicators of the unseen world...

24
00:02:49,792 --> 00:02:51,184
Yoon Ha Ru!

25
00:02:51,184 --> 00:02:53,384
Faster!

26
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:56,086
Come on!

27
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,867
It's too heavy!

28
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:06,360
We'll start over if I catch you!

29
00:03:07,221 --> 00:03:08,721
Come on!

30
00:03:09,379 --> 00:03:11,099
Faster, faster!

31
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:13,462
Perfected? What a liar!

32
00:03:26,586 --> 00:03:28,050
I don't like this at all.

33
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:29,334
That's not how you do it.

34
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:30,573
You need to use sudden force!

35
00:03:30,573 --> 00:03:32,057
Sudden, get it?

36
00:03:32,057 --> 00:03:33,521
Yoon Ha Ru.

37
00:03:33,521 --> 00:03:35,796
Flip your opponent over like this.

38
00:03:35,796 --> 00:03:37,026
Sudden force, see.

39
00:03:37,026 --> 00:03:38,743
This is how you do it.

40
00:03:38,743 --> 00:03:40,887
Give it some more oomph.

41
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:43,558
Were you starved as a kid? Why are you so weak?

42
00:03:46,692 --> 00:03:49,123
The sun's going to set at this rate!

43
00:03:49,123 --> 00:03:50,825
Hurry, let's wrap this up.

44
00:03:50,825 --> 00:03:52,155
Get up, come on!

45
00:03:52,155 --> 00:03:53,980
- Let's go.
- We're almost there, come on!

46
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,480
Let's go!

47
00:04:20,244 --> 00:04:21,744
Thanks.

48
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:32,871
- They believed in the power of nature
- Jung Woo Jae...

49
00:04:32,871 --> 00:04:35,130
- and prayed for communal prosperity
- starts judo again...

50
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:37,673
- via rituals.
- made it into the national team...

51
00:04:37,673 --> 00:04:38,813
That is why the leader of that era...

52
00:04:38,813 --> 00:04:41,419
- Okay, that's done.
- was not only a king of the people...

53
00:04:41,419 --> 00:04:43,748
but a bridge between the gods and humans.

54
00:04:43,748 --> 00:04:45,967
Like a shaman.

55
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:48,830
Can I really trust Yoon Ha Na?

56
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,898
- I hope she doesn't screw up.
- When the soul leaves the body,

57
00:04:50,898 --> 00:04:54,499
they believed the body to be an empty husk.

58
00:04:55,468 --> 00:04:59,656
So, if the husk
got taken over by a stray soul...

59
00:04:59,656 --> 00:05:01,379
or got lost,

60
00:05:01,379 --> 00:05:03,301
what did they do?

61
00:05:08,058 --> 00:05:12,203
[Shaman]
Back then, to them, shamans and rituals...

62
00:05:12,203 --> 00:05:14,124
were like the doctors of the present times.

63
00:05:14,124 --> 00:05:15,125
It was healing.

64
00:05:15,125 --> 00:05:17,472
They believed shamans
to be pathfinders for spirits.

65
00:05:17,472 --> 00:05:19,253
A spiritual guide, so to speak.

66
00:05:19,253 --> 00:05:20,909
Sir!

67
00:05:20,909 --> 00:05:22,461
What is it, Yoon Ha Na?

68
00:05:22,461 --> 00:05:24,199
It's rare that you have a question.

69
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,063
That "spiritual guide" stuff...

70
00:05:26,063 --> 00:05:28,642
Do you think it could still fly
in our present day?

71
00:05:28,642 --> 00:05:30,835
Well, historically speaking...

72
00:05:30,835 --> 00:05:32,503
the form may have changed,

73
00:05:32,503 --> 00:05:35,250
but the idea of spirituality still exists, yes.

74
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:38,043
It's a cultural tradition, you see.

75
00:05:39,638 --> 00:05:40,860
Why?

76
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:43,480
Do you want to know the future?
Thinking of going to a fortune teller?

77
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:46,356
No, nothing like that.

78
00:05:46,356 --> 00:05:49,862
Well, just the fact that
Yoon Ha Na is awake during class...

79
00:05:49,862 --> 00:05:52,805
- is enough to make me happy.
- A spiritual guide...

80
00:05:52,805 --> 00:05:54,521
Now, another point to be mindful of...

81
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:56,369
- Not bad.
- Can anyone tell me what it is?

82
00:05:56,369 --> 00:05:57,770
The seasonal rituals of the Three Hans.

83
00:05:57,770 --> 00:05:59,308
- A spiritual...
- Every December,

84
00:05:59,308 --> 00:06:00,402
- guide...
- there was a ritual called Yeonggo.

85
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:02,196
Which nation was that?

86
00:06:07,074 --> 00:06:09,274
All done.

87
00:06:15,377 --> 00:06:17,822
It'll get better soon, I guess.

88
00:06:20,012 --> 00:06:21,013
Can't you knock?

89
00:06:21,013 --> 00:06:22,386
Who cares if I saw?

90
00:06:22,386 --> 00:06:24,626
It's my body, anyway.

91
00:06:24,626 --> 00:06:27,851
It's just a sore muscle, no need for all that.

92
00:06:27,851 --> 00:06:29,935
What a weakling.

93
00:06:30,565 --> 00:06:31,566
What do you want?

94
00:06:31,566 --> 00:06:34,618
Yeah, we need to have an emergency meeting.

95
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,101
Are you certain?

96
00:06:38,101 --> 00:06:39,102
Of what?

97
00:06:39,102 --> 00:06:41,768
The trials. Are you?

98
00:06:42,393 --> 00:06:44,320
I'm doing my best.

99
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,543
That's not enough.

100
00:06:45,543 --> 00:06:49,342
My body may be a gift from the skies above,

101
00:06:49,342 --> 00:06:54,366
but you lack the software
to make use of the top-tier hardware.

102
00:06:55,087 --> 00:06:57,123
Top-tier? You've got to be kidding me.

103
00:06:57,123 --> 00:06:58,446
Well? Any good ideas?

104
00:06:58,446 --> 00:07:01,751
Personal training. Starting today.

105
00:07:01,751 --> 00:07:03,688
Personal training?

106
00:07:22,970 --> 00:07:24,583
<i>Check back into the dorms starting tomorrow.</i>

107
00:07:24,583 --> 00:07:27,189
<i>Good job, and good luck.</i>

108
00:07:50,625 --> 00:07:52,173
See, judo is all about aura.

109
00:07:52,173 --> 00:07:55,864
Once you get a grip,
you use your "you're dead meat" stare.

110
00:07:55,864 --> 00:07:57,432
Like so.

111
00:08:06,614 --> 00:08:08,775
Hey, it's late now.

112
00:08:08,775 --> 00:08:11,226
You'll wake up all our neighbors.

113
00:08:11,934 --> 00:08:16,376
The ferocity of a judo player
knows no rest, day or night! It's on 24/7!

114
00:08:16,376 --> 00:08:18,521
Yeah, yeah, sure.

115
00:08:18,521 --> 00:08:20,203
Where are your eyes? I said look here!

116
00:08:20,203 --> 00:08:22,381
You need to win
the staring contest first, okay?

117
00:08:22,381 --> 00:08:24,332
See the fire in my eyes, huh?

118
00:08:24,332 --> 00:08:26,223
Beat me, come on!

119
00:08:28,509 --> 00:08:31,492
I don't know about the fire...

120
00:08:31,492 --> 00:08:33,345
but I see your eye boogers.

121
00:08:33,345 --> 00:08:34,732
Ugh, seriously!

122
00:08:34,732 --> 00:08:38,372
My fierceness, resilience and my toughness...

123
00:08:38,372 --> 00:08:40,216
are nowhere to be found.

124
00:08:40,216 --> 00:08:45,205
Is this truly the end
of my life as a judo player?

125
00:08:49,772 --> 00:08:52,246
Why is he texting me instead of just coming in?

126
00:08:52,246 --> 00:08:54,462
- Woo Jae?
- Yeah.

127
00:08:54,462 --> 00:08:55,662
Huh?

128
00:08:55,662 --> 00:08:58,964
Why is he asking me to go see a movie?

129
00:08:59,642 --> 00:09:01,425
A movie?

130
00:09:01,425 --> 00:09:03,280
<i>Ha Na, do you have time tomorrow?</i>

131
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,762
<i>Do you want to go see a movie with me?</i>

132
00:09:04,762 --> 00:09:07,081
So, what's happening right now is...

133
00:09:07,081 --> 00:09:08,442
he's not asking me...

134
00:09:08,442 --> 00:09:10,762
but you, right?

135
00:09:10,762 --> 00:09:13,437
Well, I think so.

136
00:09:54,642 --> 00:09:57,391
<i>Okay! Can Yoon Ha Ru come, too?</i>

137
00:09:57,391 --> 00:09:58,765
<i>By the way, why not come inside?</i>

138
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:01,200
Why is he getting in the way?

139
00:10:02,232 --> 00:10:04,187
This is not going well.

140
00:10:11,201 --> 00:10:12,308
Wait, no.

141
00:10:12,308 --> 00:10:14,772
This is my chance to make things clear.

142
00:10:22,846 --> 00:10:24,778
<i>Alright, the three of us it is, then.</i>

143
00:10:24,778 --> 00:10:26,425
<i>I'm heading in now.</i>

144
00:10:31,441 --> 00:10:33,422
[Banana milk]

145
00:10:33,422 --> 00:10:35,405
It's Yoon Ha Na.

146
00:10:35,405 --> 00:10:37,918
The one I really like is...

147
00:10:37,918 --> 00:10:39,511
Yoon Ha Na.

148
00:10:40,488 --> 00:10:42,675
Yoon Ha Na, Yoon Ha Na...

149
00:10:42,675 --> 00:10:44,232
Yoon Ha Na.

150
00:10:50,045 --> 00:10:51,932
What's taking Ha Ru so long?

151
00:10:51,932 --> 00:10:53,907
What a pain in my foot.

152
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,003
Let's go.

153
00:11:01,179 --> 00:11:05,284
You... can't be serious
about going out like this.

154
00:11:05,284 --> 00:11:06,599
I am.

155
00:11:06,599 --> 00:11:08,331
What's wrong?

156
00:11:09,430 --> 00:11:10,431
Get inside.

157
00:11:10,431 --> 00:11:11,432
Where?

158
00:11:11,432 --> 00:11:12,922
Your room, come on! Hurry!

159
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:13,951
- Go inside.
- What, why?

160
00:11:13,951 --> 00:11:15,477
- Inside, now.
- Why?

161
00:11:17,682 --> 00:11:19,359
Stand up straight.

162
00:11:19,359 --> 00:11:21,180
You want me to wear this?

163
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,212
Shut it.

164
00:11:27,668 --> 00:11:29,840
This seems to fit nicely.

165
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,650
I'm not wearing a dress!

166
00:11:31,650 --> 00:11:33,188
Hey!

167
00:11:34,075 --> 00:11:35,884
Stay still.

168
00:11:54,138 --> 00:11:55,519
Come here.

169
00:12:00,597 --> 00:12:02,345
Ugh, you...

170
00:12:02,345 --> 00:12:04,030
I said, come here.

171
00:12:07,679 --> 00:12:10,206
- All done.
- It's over, right?

172
00:12:13,047 --> 00:12:14,261
Sit down.

173
00:12:14,261 --> 00:12:15,345
Why?

174
00:12:15,345 --> 00:12:16,800
I said, sit!

175
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,625
Why?

176
00:12:19,945 --> 00:12:21,626
You're not leaving like that.

177
00:12:34,518 --> 00:12:36,018
Over here.

178
00:12:51,839 --> 00:12:53,545
Damn it.

179
00:12:54,978 --> 00:12:57,508
What is wrong with him?

180
00:12:57,508 --> 00:12:58,898
Where's Jung Woo Jae?

181
00:12:58,898 --> 00:13:00,691
He's right outside.

182
00:13:00,691 --> 00:13:02,348
Do you have to walk like that?

183
00:13:02,348 --> 00:13:04,501
Just be normal for once. Please?

184
00:13:04,501 --> 00:13:06,250
I'm begging you.

185
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,091
No, hear this.

186
00:13:08,822 --> 00:13:10,522
Something's off.

187
00:13:10,522 --> 00:13:12,232
Off?

188
00:13:12,232 --> 00:13:14,586
I'm constantly feeling this
gentle breeze down there.

189
00:13:14,586 --> 00:13:16,964
It's like something's missing.

190
00:13:16,964 --> 00:13:18,847
It's unsettling.

191
00:13:19,899 --> 00:13:22,311
Can you please keep your legs together?

192
00:13:22,311 --> 00:13:24,348
I should sue you for defamation!

193
00:13:24,348 --> 00:13:26,812
Ugh, alright, alright.

194
00:13:32,948 --> 00:13:34,548
Oh, Jung Woo Jae!

195
00:13:45,747 --> 00:13:48,262
What took you so long?

196
00:13:48,262 --> 00:13:49,935
I was at the convenience store.

197
00:13:53,344 --> 00:13:55,658
Let's go inside, Woo Jae.

198
00:13:55,658 --> 00:13:57,884
Uh, okay.

199
00:14:09,194 --> 00:14:10,531
Ha Na.

200
00:14:10,531 --> 00:14:11,741
Have this.

201
00:14:11,741 --> 00:14:14,577
Milk? At the movies?

202
00:14:14,577 --> 00:14:16,951
Is this why you were late?

203
00:14:16,951 --> 00:14:20,313
Yeah, I noticed that you drink this a lot.

204
00:14:20,313 --> 00:14:21,851
Coke is the best for watching movies.

205
00:14:21,851 --> 00:14:24,126
We're not kids, who's drinking milk?

206
00:14:26,904 --> 00:14:28,444
I guess so...

207
00:14:29,239 --> 00:14:30,804
I'll drink it.

208
00:14:32,765 --> 00:14:34,479
That banana milk...

209
00:14:34,479 --> 00:14:35,600
I want it.

210
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,100
Give it to me.

211
00:14:39,951 --> 00:14:41,571
Okay.

212
00:15:09,234 --> 00:15:11,654
<i>That's so funny.</i>

213
00:15:24,626 --> 00:15:26,868
<i>So hilarious.</i>

214
00:15:32,349 --> 00:15:33,891
<i>Thanks.</i>

215
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,438
Private Yoon Ha Ru, reporting for duty!

216
00:16:14,141 --> 00:16:15,267
What is wrong with you? Sit down!

217
00:16:15,267 --> 00:16:16,779
Sorry.

218
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:29,666
God, I hate him so much!

219
00:16:39,249 --> 00:16:44,880
<i>♪ I'll wait through countless mishaps ♪</i>

220
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:50,636
<i>♪ I'll smile through all the pain ♪</i>

221
00:16:50,636 --> 00:17:01,103
<i>♪ Don't leave, don't give up yet ♪</i>

222
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:07,404
<i>♪ See this love grow deeper
the more you push me away ♪</i>

223
00:17:07,404 --> 00:17:12,929
<i>♪ You can hold my tongue,
but the world will still know ♪</i>

224
00:17:12,929 --> 00:17:15,475
<i>♪ So why are you the only one clueless? ♪</i>

225
00:17:15,475 --> 00:17:22,020
<i>♪ Why don't you see the man
who will keep you safe? ♪</i>

226
00:17:26,050 --> 00:17:29,639
- I ate that up!
<i>- Practice harder and try for a perfect score!</i>

227
00:17:34,713 --> 00:17:36,164
<i>♪ You ♪</i>

228
00:17:36,164 --> 00:17:39,268
<i>♪ When I fall down ♪</i>

229
00:17:39,268 --> 00:17:44,350
<i>♪ Don't waver, help me up time and time again ♪</i>

230
00:17:44,350 --> 00:17:47,818
<i>♪ With your strong gaze ♪</i>

231
00:17:47,818 --> 00:17:49,611
<i>♪ And you ♪</i>

232
00:17:49,611 --> 00:17:52,906
<i>♪ When I'm having a hard time ♪</i>

233
00:17:52,906 --> 00:17:56,010
<i>♪ You came for me to the edge of the cliff ♪</i>

234
00:17:56,010 --> 00:17:57,744
<i>♪ Without fail ♪</i>

235
00:17:57,744 --> 00:18:01,744
<i>♪ And held my two hands in yours ♪</i>

236
00:18:01,744 --> 00:18:06,255
<i>♪ Though I have nothing to offer ♪</i>

237
00:18:06,255 --> 00:18:08,833
<i>♪ Nothing to show ♪</i>

238
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:11,512
<i>♪ But today, for you ♪</i>

239
00:18:11,512 --> 00:18:14,970
<i>♪ I sing this song ♪</i>

240
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:16,434
<i>♪ Tonight ♪</i>

241
00:18:16,434 --> 00:18:20,065
<i>♪ In your two eyes ♪</i>

242
00:18:20,065 --> 00:18:22,498
<i>Take a break, Ha Na.</i>

243
00:18:22,498 --> 00:18:23,499
<i>Like you did?</i>

244
00:18:23,499 --> 00:18:25,818
<i>Like when you gave up judo?</i>

245
00:18:25,818 --> 00:18:28,815
<i>But what do you get after running away?</i>

246
00:18:28,815 --> 00:18:31,164
<i>You ended up a bodyguard.</i>

247
00:18:33,588 --> 00:18:34,612
<i>Don't be scared.</i>

248
00:18:34,612 --> 00:18:36,772
<i>Just be yourself.</i>

249
00:18:36,772 --> 00:18:38,883
<i>To me, no one shines brighter...</i>

250
00:18:38,883 --> 00:18:41,089
<i>than you, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

251
00:18:42,004 --> 00:18:43,690
<i>Thank goodness...</i>

252
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:44,691
<i>Woo Jae!</i>

253
00:18:44,691 --> 00:18:46,543
<i>No, wait!</i>

254
00:18:47,316 --> 00:18:48,754
<i>What do I do?</i>

255
00:18:48,754 --> 00:18:51,733
<i>♪ Never say goodbye ♪</i>

256
00:18:51,733 --> 00:18:53,805
<i>♪ Because this world, to me ♪</i>

257
00:18:53,805 --> 00:18:57,260
<i>♪ is only you and I ♪</i>

258
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,589
Oh, my throat hurts.
I'm going to the convenience store.

259
00:19:45,589 --> 00:19:46,865
Are you guys going?

260
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:48,906
I'm good.

261
00:19:48,906 --> 00:19:50,769
We'll wait for you.

262
00:20:07,275 --> 00:20:09,617
Hey. Why the long face?

263
00:20:10,357 --> 00:20:11,857
No reason.

264
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,804
Just thinking about someone.

265
00:20:15,898 --> 00:20:17,238
Who?

266
00:20:17,878 --> 00:20:19,896
Just someone.

267
00:20:19,896 --> 00:20:21,792
Not the sharpest tool in the shed.

268
00:20:22,677 --> 00:20:24,652
Well, who is it?

269
00:20:31,231 --> 00:20:33,844
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

270
00:21:08,943 --> 00:21:10,471
What are you guys doing?

271
00:21:13,159 --> 00:21:15,928
It was buy two, get one. Big bro is buying!
Want one?

272
00:21:15,928 --> 00:21:18,021
Oh, I'm good.

273
00:21:18,021 --> 00:21:19,425
Want it?

274
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:32,709
<i>I must be out of my mind.</i>

275
00:21:32,709 --> 00:21:34,503
<i>What is wrong with me?</i>

276
00:21:34,503 --> 00:21:36,631
<i>Get it together, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

277
00:21:40,037 --> 00:21:42,203
<i>The person I like is...</i>

278
00:21:43,389 --> 00:21:44,944
Yoon Ha Na.

279
00:21:46,348 --> 00:21:47,766
You know...

280
00:21:47,766 --> 00:21:49,170
Yeah?

281
00:21:50,102 --> 00:21:52,810
I... actually, I...

282
00:21:54,091 --> 00:21:56,116
Yeah, what is it? Spit it out.

283
00:22:00,112 --> 00:22:02,096
I like you!

284
00:22:04,418 --> 00:22:05,784
Huh?

285
00:22:05,784 --> 00:22:07,306
What?

286
00:22:09,264 --> 00:22:10,632
I...

287
00:22:11,370 --> 00:22:13,870
I like you.

288
00:22:28,223 --> 00:22:31,020
Jung Woo Jae, you idiot...

289
00:22:32,905 --> 00:22:35,153
How is that a proper confession?

290
00:22:35,153 --> 00:22:36,761
In what world was that a good idea?

291
00:22:36,761 --> 00:22:38,949
Why did I do that
in front of a convenience store?

292
00:22:41,347 --> 00:22:42,973
<i>Yoon Ha Na.</i>

293
00:22:43,691 --> 00:22:46,064
<i>I... actually, I...</i>

294
00:22:47,492 --> 00:22:50,052
<i>I like you!</i>

295
00:22:51,138 --> 00:22:52,247
<i>Huh?</i>

296
00:22:52,247 --> 00:22:53,635
<i>What?</i>

297
00:23:06,553 --> 00:23:09,190
Why did it have to be then?

298
00:23:09,190 --> 00:23:10,541
Why right then?

299
00:23:10,541 --> 00:23:13,309
Why?

300
00:23:14,865 --> 00:23:17,552
Oh, man, what do I do?

301
00:23:17,552 --> 00:23:21,084
Wow, he just confessed to me!

302
00:23:21,084 --> 00:23:22,718
He did it to me, not you.

303
00:23:22,718 --> 00:23:24,835
Well, it's me now!

304
00:23:24,835 --> 00:23:26,726
Think about it, what if he tried to, like,

305
00:23:26,726 --> 00:23:28,771
kiss me, or something?

306
00:23:28,771 --> 00:23:30,704
Oh, I'm about to throw up.

307
00:23:30,704 --> 00:23:33,354
God, can you stay still for a minute?

308
00:23:33,354 --> 00:23:34,657
You saw it too, didn't you?

309
00:23:34,657 --> 00:23:36,186
You saw the way he looked at me, right?

310
00:23:36,186 --> 00:23:39,381
It was so intense, I thought I'd melt!

311
00:23:39,381 --> 00:23:42,700
It's not just my problem, though.
How would you feel?

312
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:45,543
Imagine him and me holding hands...

313
00:23:45,543 --> 00:23:46,825
and hugging...

314
00:23:46,825 --> 00:23:48,612
- and kissing...
- Stop!

315
00:23:50,556 --> 00:23:52,315
Oh, seriously.

316
00:23:53,328 --> 00:23:56,770
<i>Shamans and rituals were like
the doctors of the present times.</i>

317
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:57,771
<i>It was healing.</i>

318
00:23:57,771 --> 00:24:00,107
<i>They believed shamans to be
pathfinders for spirits.</i>

319
00:24:00,107 --> 00:24:02,433
<i>A spiritual guide, so to speak.</i>

320
00:24:02,433 --> 00:24:05,304
Hey, let's switch.

321
00:24:05,304 --> 00:24:07,844
- What?
- Our bodies.

322
00:24:07,844 --> 00:24:09,343
So, go back to the future?

323
00:24:09,343 --> 00:24:10,394
We can't, not yet.

324
00:24:10,394 --> 00:24:12,648
We need to see Woo Jae make the national team.

325
00:24:12,648 --> 00:24:13,999
No, right now.

326
00:24:13,999 --> 00:24:16,317
Let's swap right here, right now.

327
00:24:16,317 --> 00:24:19,083
- Huh?
- Well, we haven't tried anything.

328
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:20,663
That's because that doesn't make sense!

329
00:24:20,663 --> 00:24:22,824
Well, does this right now make sense to you?

330
00:24:22,824 --> 00:24:25,021
We've already been swapped,
there's no logic to this!

331
00:24:25,021 --> 00:24:27,230
It makes no sense!

332
00:24:27,230 --> 00:24:29,773
- Well, yeah, I guess so.
- Let's try it.

333
00:24:29,773 --> 00:24:32,061
I'm desperate, please!

334
00:24:32,848 --> 00:24:36,485
Are you seriously worried
that he might kiss you?

335
00:24:39,354 --> 00:24:41,283
It's about judo.

336
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:43,161
Huh?

337
00:24:43,161 --> 00:24:44,890
The trials!

338
00:24:44,890 --> 00:24:47,213
There's not much time left.

339
00:24:48,752 --> 00:24:51,128
He's obviously going to make it in.

340
00:24:51,128 --> 00:24:52,700
But, well...

341
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:54,892
I need to at least come in 2nd place.

342
00:24:57,381 --> 00:24:59,000
Yoon Ha Ru...

343
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,637
You were really worried.

344
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:04,774
I shouldn't be pressuring you
as your big brother.

345
00:25:04,774 --> 00:25:06,893
Sorry about that.

346
00:25:06,893 --> 00:25:08,068
No.

347
00:25:08,068 --> 00:25:09,597
Let's try.

348
00:25:10,307 --> 00:25:12,076
The sooner, the better.

349
00:25:12,076 --> 00:25:13,369
Okay.

350
00:25:14,658 --> 00:25:16,171
So...

351
00:25:16,770 --> 00:25:19,046
How are we doing this?

352
00:25:21,219 --> 00:25:22,594
Shamanism.

353
00:25:22,594 --> 00:25:24,611
Shamanism?

354
00:25:54,717 --> 00:25:56,537
Sis!

355
00:25:56,537 --> 00:25:59,039
You're standing on the edge of a cliff, sis.

356
00:25:59,039 --> 00:26:02,749
One more step and it all crumbles.

357
00:26:02,749 --> 00:26:05,276
That tower that you worked so hard on building.

358
00:26:05,276 --> 00:26:06,732
Pardon?

359
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:08,399
There's no use pretending.

360
00:26:08,399 --> 00:26:10,668
Your insides are all burnt black.

361
00:26:10,668 --> 00:26:12,583
It's just ashes in there.

362
00:26:12,583 --> 00:26:14,432
How did you know?

363
00:26:15,439 --> 00:26:18,821
And with you, mister...

364
00:26:28,159 --> 00:26:29,959
Who are you?

365
00:26:29,959 --> 00:26:33,544
Who are you, you fox!

366
00:26:33,544 --> 00:26:36,683
Some wretch has taken over your body.

367
00:26:37,896 --> 00:26:40,117
Who? Who is it?

368
00:26:44,018 --> 00:26:46,551
Oh my, Grandmama...

369
00:26:46,551 --> 00:26:48,657
You like it there, don't you!

370
00:26:48,657 --> 00:26:50,331
He's young,

371
00:26:50,331 --> 00:26:52,037
and handsome...

372
00:26:52,037 --> 00:26:55,200
he's a great source of energy.

373
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,847
There's no place better, huh?

374
00:26:56,847 --> 00:26:58,611
You love it, don't you!

375
00:27:03,919 --> 00:27:06,291
Grandmama likes it in you.

376
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:09,687
She looks like she wants to stay.

377
00:27:09,687 --> 00:27:11,590
So, an old lady? Who is she?

378
00:27:11,590 --> 00:27:16,094
Sis, your troubles are also because
this hag is in your twin brother.

379
00:27:16,094 --> 00:27:19,556
You're twins, so it takes double the effort.

380
00:27:19,556 --> 00:27:21,220
Double...

381
00:27:21,220 --> 00:27:23,285
the effort.

382
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:26,144
Well, how much will it cost?

383
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:27,659
10 million won!

384
00:27:28,782 --> 00:27:29,783
It's a rip-off.

385
00:27:29,783 --> 00:27:30,995
10 million?

386
00:27:30,995 --> 00:27:32,288
Yes.

387
00:27:32,881 --> 00:27:34,733
Should we ask Mom?

388
00:27:38,835 --> 00:27:40,176
Hey.

389
00:27:45,067 --> 00:27:46,476
Hey!

390
00:27:57,648 --> 00:27:59,133
Kiddo.

391
00:28:03,034 --> 00:28:04,534
Is it you?

392
00:28:05,192 --> 00:28:08,314
The one who's selling my name
to rip people off?

393
00:28:10,011 --> 00:28:11,788
You... you're lying.

394
00:28:13,768 --> 00:28:15,780
Open your eyes.

395
00:28:15,780 --> 00:28:17,307
Grandma?

396
00:28:17,307 --> 00:28:19,665
Are... are you actually there?

397
00:28:23,471 --> 00:28:26,923
How low can you go, ripping money off of kids?

398
00:28:26,923 --> 00:28:27,924
Kiddo.

399
00:28:27,924 --> 00:28:30,036
If you keep using that money
to satiate your own greed,

400
00:28:30,036 --> 00:28:32,254
your guardian spirit will get mad
and leave you for good.

401
00:28:32,254 --> 00:28:34,542
No use crying about it to me when it happens.

402
00:28:34,542 --> 00:28:36,210
No... no way.

403
00:28:36,210 --> 00:28:38,201
It's not really her.

404
00:28:40,787 --> 00:28:42,747
Which hag are you! Who are you!

405
00:28:42,747 --> 00:28:45,065
Stop it with the hag!

406
00:28:52,493 --> 00:28:53,839
Hey...

407
00:28:56,820 --> 00:28:57,821
Yeah.

408
00:28:57,821 --> 00:28:59,564
My grandma says...

409
00:28:59,564 --> 00:29:01,421
if you keep calling her a hag,

410
00:29:01,421 --> 00:29:05,027
I should rip your tongue out
and throw it at the tapestry over there.

411
00:29:05,027 --> 00:29:07,540
Do you want to see her angry?

412
00:29:10,048 --> 00:29:11,262
Get those hands off the table!

413
00:29:11,262 --> 00:29:13,532
I will, I am, I have!

414
00:29:14,721 --> 00:29:16,954
I won't, I'm sorry, please! Just leave!

415
00:29:16,954 --> 00:29:19,240
Please, leave!

416
00:29:20,333 --> 00:29:22,567
Leave!

417
00:29:22,567 --> 00:29:23,911
"Spiritual guide," my foot.

418
00:29:23,911 --> 00:29:25,154
We're broke high schoolers! 10 million?

419
00:29:25,154 --> 00:29:26,332
And out of mom's pockets, no less?

420
00:29:26,332 --> 00:29:29,791
Your brain must've gone back in time as well.

421
00:29:30,771 --> 00:29:31,795
Have you lost it?

422
00:29:31,795 --> 00:29:34,849
Isn't it the effort that counts?

423
00:29:34,849 --> 00:29:36,183
If you hit me now,

424
00:29:36,183 --> 00:29:38,620
you're just a dude hitting a girl!

425
00:29:42,904 --> 00:29:44,867
- Wait up!
- Screw off.

426
00:29:44,867 --> 00:29:46,223
Why?

427
00:29:46,223 --> 00:29:47,439
I said, bugger off!

428
00:29:47,439 --> 00:29:49,498
Wait for me!

429
00:30:10,807 --> 00:30:12,429
Yoon Ha Na.

430
00:30:13,299 --> 00:30:15,098
What?

431
00:30:16,024 --> 00:30:18,760
That wasn't very big-brotherly of me
to put you under pressure.

432
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,260
Sorry.

433
00:30:20,934 --> 00:30:22,740
Whatever.

434
00:30:22,740 --> 00:30:25,474
I wasn't thinking hard enough.

435
00:30:25,474 --> 00:30:26,749
And now I realize

436
00:30:26,749 --> 00:30:29,039
that I need to think even less.

437
00:30:30,518 --> 00:30:31,965
- What?
- See.

438
00:30:31,965 --> 00:30:33,595
Let's think simply.

439
00:30:33,595 --> 00:30:35,620
The very reason we're here...

440
00:30:35,620 --> 00:30:37,127
is Jung Woo Jae.

441
00:30:37,127 --> 00:30:39,055
Not my trials.

442
00:30:39,767 --> 00:30:41,134
So?

443
00:30:41,134 --> 00:30:43,070
Saving Woo Jae comes first.

444
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:45,321
Let's see him make it into the team,

445
00:30:45,321 --> 00:30:47,081
and return to the present.

446
00:30:47,740 --> 00:30:49,573
What about you?

447
00:30:49,573 --> 00:30:50,774
What about it?

448
00:30:50,774 --> 00:30:52,299
I've been a judo player my whole life.

449
00:30:52,299 --> 00:30:55,286
Missing my shot at this one trial
won't spell out the end for me.

450
00:30:56,824 --> 00:30:59,061
Oh, come on, it's fine.

451
00:30:59,061 --> 00:31:00,637
Go on, go!

452
00:31:06,826 --> 00:31:11,371
I'll... do my best.

453
00:31:11,371 --> 00:31:13,625
Yoon Ha Ru, your life...

454
00:31:15,023 --> 00:31:17,007
I'll protect it as well.

455
00:31:23,443 --> 00:31:25,134
- But...
- What now?

456
00:31:25,134 --> 00:31:27,177
Jung Woo Jae.

457
00:31:27,177 --> 00:31:28,543
What do we do with him?

458
00:31:28,543 --> 00:31:29,963
Huh?

459
00:31:30,599 --> 00:31:32,478
It's fine.

460
00:31:33,238 --> 00:31:35,012
It's not fine.

461
00:31:35,937 --> 00:31:37,537
It's fine.

462
00:31:38,210 --> 00:31:40,310
It's not fine.

463
00:31:41,250 --> 00:31:42,850
It's fine...

464
00:31:47,862 --> 00:31:49,126
<i>I like you!</i>

465
00:31:49,126 --> 00:31:51,537
<i>Huh? What?</i>

466
00:31:58,126 --> 00:31:59,715
It's not fine.

467
00:31:59,715 --> 00:32:01,576
Not at all.

468
00:32:01,576 --> 00:32:04,856
This is driving me nuts!

469
00:32:21,043 --> 00:32:22,348
Come on!

470
00:32:22,348 --> 00:32:24,510
Alright, I'm going.

471
00:32:24,510 --> 00:32:25,986
Don't mess around, okay?

472
00:32:25,986 --> 00:32:29,867
I got it, stop treating me like an idiot!

473
00:32:31,368 --> 00:32:34,044
- Go on!
- I said alright!

474
00:32:37,504 --> 00:32:39,049
Yoon Ha Ru!

475
00:32:41,151 --> 00:32:42,931
Go, go!

476
00:33:02,630 --> 00:33:04,900
Ha Na.

477
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:06,351
Hi.

478
00:33:19,209 --> 00:33:20,876
- I...
- I...

479
00:33:25,724 --> 00:33:27,407
You go first.

480
00:33:27,407 --> 00:33:28,633
Okay.

481
00:33:28,633 --> 00:33:30,163
Well...

482
00:33:30,163 --> 00:33:34,618
About... what you said last night.

483
00:33:35,259 --> 00:33:37,110
Oh, that.

484
00:33:37,996 --> 00:33:39,436
I must've freaked you out.

485
00:33:39,436 --> 00:33:42,156
Yeah, for real, it freaked me...

486
00:33:45,096 --> 00:33:48,841
Well, it was a bit surprising, I guess.

487
00:33:49,958 --> 00:33:51,318
But...

488
00:33:52,420 --> 00:33:54,687
Well, what I meant to say is...

489
00:33:54,687 --> 00:33:56,218
I...

490
00:34:05,679 --> 00:34:07,327
Thank you.

491
00:34:08,737 --> 00:34:09,738
Huh?

492
00:34:09,738 --> 00:34:12,077
For feeling that way towards me.

493
00:34:12,077 --> 00:34:13,601
Thanks.

494
00:34:16,403 --> 00:34:19,431
It's nothing, really.

495
00:34:21,581 --> 00:34:23,897
The thing is, though...

496
00:34:23,897 --> 00:34:25,397
I, uh...

497
00:34:28,953 --> 00:34:30,818
Right now,

498
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:34,126
you're about to face a very important trial.

499
00:34:34,715 --> 00:34:38,401
I need to study for my college entrance, too.

500
00:34:39,164 --> 00:34:40,304
Yeah.

501
00:34:40,304 --> 00:34:42,094
Which is why I think...

502
00:34:42,094 --> 00:34:43,603
I get what you mean.

503
00:34:43,603 --> 00:34:44,627
Huh?

504
00:34:44,627 --> 00:34:45,829
No, wait.

505
00:34:45,829 --> 00:34:48,350
- I'm not finished...
- You're right, Ha Na.

506
00:34:48,939 --> 00:34:51,827
I was being too rash.

507
00:34:52,926 --> 00:34:57,786
I wanted to wait until after the trials
to properly confess to you.

508
00:34:58,703 --> 00:35:00,225
That day was a mistake.

509
00:35:00,225 --> 00:35:01,399
Hey, no.

510
00:35:01,399 --> 00:35:03,689
Don't call it a mistake.

511
00:35:05,047 --> 00:35:07,092
I'll confess to you again, properly...

512
00:35:07,092 --> 00:35:09,380
after the trials.

513
00:35:10,410 --> 00:35:11,870
When I make the national team,

514
00:35:11,870 --> 00:35:14,037
and you get admitted to your dream college...

515
00:35:14,037 --> 00:35:15,896
we'll talk again.

516
00:35:15,896 --> 00:35:17,783
Oh, yeah.

517
00:35:17,783 --> 00:35:19,654
Okay, let's do that.

518
00:35:19,654 --> 00:35:21,547
Yeah, I like the sound of that.

519
00:35:21,547 --> 00:35:23,357
Thank you for starting
this conversation with me.

520
00:35:23,357 --> 00:35:24,711
Oh, it's nothing.

521
00:35:24,711 --> 00:35:26,319
No need to thank me.

522
00:35:31,265 --> 00:35:32,864
That's a relief.

523
00:35:38,890 --> 00:35:40,757
It's settled, then.

524
00:35:40,757 --> 00:35:42,313
Now...

525
00:35:42,313 --> 00:35:44,619
let's just focus on him
making it into the team.

526
00:35:46,250 --> 00:35:47,847
[National team trials, D-15]

527
00:36:24,334 --> 00:36:26,980
[National team trials, D-12]

528
00:36:51,792 --> 00:36:54,430
[National team trials, D-5]

529
00:37:09,521 --> 00:37:11,414
[National team trials, D-day]
This day calls for a barbecue!

530
00:37:11,414 --> 00:37:14,211
Not pork, no, it has to be beef.

531
00:37:22,744 --> 00:37:24,622
Today's the day.

532
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:26,740
Yeah.

533
00:37:28,211 --> 00:37:29,928
Let's give it our best.

534
00:37:29,928 --> 00:37:32,074
Yeah, let's do this.

535
00:37:36,653 --> 00:37:38,955
- Everyone on board?
- Yes, sir!

536
00:37:41,141 --> 00:37:43,749
Today's dinner...

537
00:37:43,749 --> 00:37:46,636
It's up to you whether
I pay for a chicken dinner or a beef banquet!

538
00:37:46,636 --> 00:37:48,324
Prove yourselves on the mat, got it?

539
00:37:48,324 --> 00:37:49,036
- Yes, sir!
- Okay!

540
00:37:49,036 --> 00:37:50,674
You heard him, folks!

541
00:37:50,674 --> 00:37:52,894
We'll run him bankrupt with a beef banquet!

542
00:37:52,894 --> 00:37:54,650
We'll show him what we're made of!

543
00:37:54,650 --> 00:37:57,255
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

544
00:37:57,255 --> 00:38:02,714
- Beef! Beef!
- Beef! Beef!

545
00:38:03,782 --> 00:38:07,212
Mom! We need to leave!

546
00:38:08,395 --> 00:38:12,168
Your mom always takes so long
to get ready to go anywhere ever!

547
00:38:12,168 --> 00:38:13,210
Takes a lifetime.

548
00:38:13,210 --> 00:38:16,394
Mom! Do you even know what time it is?
What if there's traffic?

549
00:38:16,394 --> 00:38:17,917
We won't be late.

550
00:38:17,917 --> 00:38:19,468
Stop fussing!

551
00:38:19,468 --> 00:38:21,154
The trials will last the whole darn day anyway.

552
00:38:21,154 --> 00:38:23,135
Well, Ha Ru will only be competing for so long.

553
00:38:23,135 --> 00:38:24,314
Come on, come on!

554
00:38:24,314 --> 00:38:26,413
- Alright, let's go!
- Let's!

555
00:38:26,413 --> 00:38:27,587
- We're leaving now!
- Let's go!

556
00:38:27,587 --> 00:38:29,334
- You've got everything, right?
- Yeah!

557
00:38:29,334 --> 00:38:31,154
- Okay, let's go!
- Go!

558
00:38:31,154 --> 00:38:32,639
Oh, wait, wait!

559
00:38:32,639 --> 00:38:33,740
What is it now?

560
00:38:33,740 --> 00:38:35,921
I forgot something! Wait!

561
00:38:35,921 --> 00:38:38,190
You're for sure your mother's daughter!

562
00:38:38,190 --> 00:38:40,686
Hush and go get the car ready!

563
00:39:00,122 --> 00:39:03,646
<i>Woo Jae, this is the day.</i>

564
00:39:03,646 --> 00:39:05,363
<i>After today,</i>

565
00:39:05,363 --> 00:39:07,563
<i>things will be different.</i>

566
00:39:22,779 --> 00:39:26,349
<i>I'll end our days of pain and anguish.</i>

567
00:39:26,992 --> 00:39:29,295
<i>I will make sure of it.</i>

568
00:39:38,792 --> 00:39:41,085
You think Ha Ru will do well?

569
00:39:41,085 --> 00:39:42,813
Of course.

570
00:39:42,813 --> 00:39:44,050
But honey, have you noticed?

571
00:39:44,050 --> 00:39:47,020
The tension today is way stronger.

572
00:39:47,020 --> 00:39:48,920
Yes, but I don't see why.

573
00:39:48,920 --> 00:39:51,428
This isn't the first time Ha Ru has competed.

574
00:39:51,428 --> 00:39:54,946
Don't you worry, Madam Jung Yeong Sook.

575
00:39:59,799 --> 00:40:02,280
<i>Don't forget to bring this tomorrow.</i>

576
00:40:02,280 --> 00:40:03,780
<i>Yeah.</i>

577
00:40:05,049 --> 00:40:09,147
<i>We'll be able to make it back tomorrow, right?</i>

578
00:40:09,870 --> 00:40:11,848
<i>We will.</i>

579
00:40:11,848 --> 00:40:14,494
<i>Woo Jae will make it in, no matter what.</i>

580
00:40:17,587 --> 00:40:18,773
<i>And me, as well...</i>

581
00:40:18,773 --> 00:40:19,774
<i>No,</i>

582
00:40:19,774 --> 00:40:21,274
<i>I mean, you...</i>

583
00:40:21,274 --> 00:40:23,402
<i>will make it, too.</i>

584
00:40:23,402 --> 00:40:25,583
<i>I'll try my absolute best.</i>

585
00:40:25,583 --> 00:40:26,815
<i>Don't exert yourself.</i>

586
00:40:26,815 --> 00:40:28,884
<i>Just don't get hurt.</i>

587
00:40:29,737 --> 00:40:31,121
<i>Okay.</i>

588
00:40:34,236 --> 00:40:36,743
Ha Ru takes after me, he'll do fine.

589
00:40:36,743 --> 00:40:39,757
Please make it in, Ha Ru...

590
00:40:39,757 --> 00:40:41,851
Oh, please, please...

591
00:40:41,851 --> 00:40:44,029
Are you even listening to me?

592
00:40:46,113 --> 00:40:47,427
[Shinil Sports Complex]

593
00:40:47,427 --> 00:40:49,650
Let's do this!

594
00:40:50,338 --> 00:40:51,854
Look at the thug.

595
00:40:51,854 --> 00:40:53,413
He's gotten even more buff!

596
00:40:53,413 --> 00:40:54,873
That's scary.

597
00:40:54,873 --> 00:40:55,874
- You scared?
- Yeah...

598
00:40:55,874 --> 00:40:56,934
That's cute.

599
00:40:56,934 --> 00:40:57,984
He's going to cry today.

600
00:40:57,984 --> 00:40:59,656
Hey, look at him.

601
00:41:02,662 --> 00:41:04,499
Well, well.

602
00:41:04,499 --> 00:41:06,174
Look who it is.

603
00:41:10,341 --> 00:41:13,041
I thought you quit judo.
Crawling back like a dog?

604
00:41:13,041 --> 00:41:14,612
Have you no shame?

605
00:41:15,720 --> 00:41:17,212
Why's that?

606
00:41:17,212 --> 00:41:19,432
Did you realize once you left the judo scene

607
00:41:19,432 --> 00:41:21,632
that you're no good for anything else?

608
00:41:28,204 --> 00:41:29,833
See you later.

609
00:41:36,590 --> 00:41:38,808
What's his problem?

610
00:41:39,805 --> 00:41:41,823
Are you okay?

611
00:41:42,683 --> 00:41:43,874
Yeah.

612
00:41:46,365 --> 00:41:47,597
Who the hell is he?

613
00:41:47,597 --> 00:41:50,110
Baekyeon High School's judo thug?

614
00:41:50,110 --> 00:41:51,111
A chick?

615
00:41:51,111 --> 00:41:53,072
That's Lee Hyeong Won.

616
00:41:54,664 --> 00:41:56,474
Lee Hyeong Won?

617
00:41:59,337 --> 00:42:00,882
Let's go.

618
00:42:02,227 --> 00:42:03,530
Okay.

619
00:42:14,493 --> 00:42:15,939
Everyone!

620
00:42:18,519 --> 00:42:20,597
You are all nameless on the mat.

621
00:42:20,597 --> 00:42:22,779
Either you are a winner or a loser.

622
00:42:22,779 --> 00:42:24,127
You'll climb off that mat
with either of those names.

623
00:42:24,127 --> 00:42:25,206
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

624
00:42:25,206 --> 00:42:27,327
I'll make it short. Just remember three things.

625
00:42:27,327 --> 00:42:30,275
Don't let go of the collar, keep eye contact,

626
00:42:30,275 --> 00:42:32,558
and... endure. Whatever it takes.

627
00:42:32,558 --> 00:42:33,524
Understood?

628
00:42:33,524 --> 00:42:35,464
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

629
00:42:36,096 --> 00:42:37,307
Today...

630
00:42:37,307 --> 00:42:39,738
we'll have that beef banquet!

631
00:42:46,176 --> 00:42:47,765
Good luck.

632
00:43:06,670 --> 00:43:08,247
There he is!

633
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:21,553
Go, Yoon Ha Ru!

634
00:43:21,553 --> 00:43:23,613
- Show them!
- Go, Yoon Ha Ru!

635
00:43:32,433 --> 00:43:33,872
Start!

636
00:43:43,788 --> 00:43:46,140
[National team trials, round of 16]
[Lee Hyeong Won : Pyo Gyeong Woo]

637
00:44:01,432 --> 00:44:03,673
Yes, that's it! Tear him apart!

638
00:44:21,284 --> 00:44:22,569
[Lee Hyeong Won]

639
00:44:23,447 --> 00:44:26,590
The judo thug, Lee Hyeong Won!

640
00:44:26,590 --> 00:44:29,883
He was talented, but he dropped off
the face of the earth one day.

641
00:44:30,760 --> 00:44:33,142
I wonder what he's doing now.

642
00:44:35,584 --> 00:44:36,889
[Jung Woo Jae : Kim Dong Gil]

643
00:44:38,959 --> 00:44:40,475
Go!

644
00:44:43,334 --> 00:44:44,539
Start!

645
00:44:52,609 --> 00:44:53,972
Good!

646
00:44:54,601 --> 00:44:56,966
That's it, Jung Woo Jae!

647
00:45:03,250 --> 00:45:04,394
[Yoon Ha Ru : Jang Won]

648
00:45:10,250 --> 00:45:11,532
Start!

649
00:45:23,169 --> 00:45:25,971
Yes, defend! Defense position, there you go!

650
00:45:34,268 --> 00:45:35,689
Stop!

651
00:45:37,713 --> 00:45:40,441
- It's okay!
- Thank goodness!

652
00:45:41,286 --> 00:45:43,486
Go, Ha Ru!

653
00:45:46,468 --> 00:45:48,533
Yoon Ha Ru!

654
00:45:48,533 --> 00:45:49,534
Don't give up!

655
00:45:49,534 --> 00:45:50,809
Don't give up yet!

656
00:45:50,809 --> 00:45:53,564
Don't you dare give up!

657
00:45:53,564 --> 00:45:55,064
Let's go!

658
00:46:01,053 --> 00:46:02,268
Start!

659
00:46:06,444 --> 00:46:09,279
- Go, go, Yoon Ha Ru!
- Go!

660
00:46:09,279 --> 00:46:11,099
Go, go!

661
00:46:11,099 --> 00:46:13,299
You're doing great!

662
00:46:20,594 --> 00:46:22,512
- Full point!
- Let's go!

663
00:46:24,824 --> 00:46:26,325
Stop!

664
00:46:26,325 --> 00:46:31,708
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

665
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:36,210
[National team trials, round of 8]
[Jung Woo Jae : Park Sung Soo]

666
00:46:41,683 --> 00:46:43,284
Pinning!

667
00:46:49,725 --> 00:46:51,144
Half point!

668
00:46:51,812 --> 00:46:53,237
Full point!

669
00:47:02,751 --> 00:47:04,289
[Round of 8]
[Yoon Ha Ru : Lee Hyeong Won]

670
00:47:11,306 --> 00:47:14,340
You dare hit Woo Jae's shoulder?

671
00:47:14,340 --> 00:47:15,393
You bastard...

672
00:47:15,393 --> 00:47:17,297
You're dead.

673
00:47:29,847 --> 00:47:31,184
Start!

674
00:47:38,090 --> 00:47:39,519
<i>I can do this!</i>

675
00:47:39,519 --> 00:47:41,645
<i>Yoon Ha Ru won all of these matches anyway.</i>

676
00:47:41,645 --> 00:47:42,742
<i>I can do this!</i>

677
00:47:42,742 --> 00:47:44,643
<i>I can protect everyone...</i>

678
00:47:51,955 --> 00:47:53,464
Are you okay?

679
00:47:54,997 --> 00:47:56,621
Go, go!

680
00:48:05,636 --> 00:48:07,001
<i>Yoon Ha Na.</i>

681
00:48:07,001 --> 00:48:08,680
<i>You can do it!</i>

682
00:48:08,680 --> 00:48:10,005
Start!

683
00:48:22,391 --> 00:48:24,655
<i>Wait, that's...</i>

684
00:48:32,649 --> 00:48:34,065
<i>Full point!</i>

685
00:48:41,908 --> 00:48:43,805
<i>That's it, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

686
00:48:50,824 --> 00:48:52,383
<i>See it through, Ha Na.</i>

687
00:48:52,383 --> 00:48:53,906
<i>Please...</i>

688
00:48:56,558 --> 00:48:58,285
<i>No, Yoon Ha Na...</i>

689
00:48:58,285 --> 00:49:00,242
<i>Do it for Ha Ru!</i>

690
00:49:00,242 --> 00:49:02,150
<i>Don't!</i>

691
00:49:02,150 --> 00:49:03,823
<i>Come on!</i>

692
00:49:28,417 --> 00:49:29,757
What's going on?

693
00:49:33,498 --> 00:49:35,496
It'll be okay.

694
00:49:36,347 --> 00:49:39,027
- Go! Check on him!
- Oh, wait...

695
00:49:46,201 --> 00:49:47,954
You'll have to go see a doctor.

696
00:49:47,954 --> 00:49:49,323
Get some tests done.

697
00:49:49,323 --> 00:49:51,534
Oh, no, my baby...

698
00:49:51,534 --> 00:49:52,989
It'll be alright.

699
00:49:52,989 --> 00:49:54,630
It's no big deal.

700
00:49:58,042 --> 00:50:00,029
[Round of 4]
[Jung Woo Jae : Lee Hyeong Won]

701
00:50:19,459 --> 00:50:20,733
Start!

702
00:50:27,980 --> 00:50:29,778
Oh, right.

703
00:50:29,778 --> 00:50:31,690
Woo Jae's semifinal will start soon...

704
00:50:31,690 --> 00:50:34,084
Oh, I'll go keep watch.

705
00:50:37,175 --> 00:50:39,578
- Another ice pack, please.
- Alright.

706
00:50:49,421 --> 00:50:53,164
- Beef banquet!
- Beef, beef, beef!

707
00:51:34,194 --> 00:51:35,444
<i>What?</i>

708
00:51:35,444 --> 00:51:36,468
<i>Lee Hyeong Won...</i>

709
00:51:36,468 --> 00:51:39,295
<i>This is how he disappeared?</i>

710
00:51:49,670 --> 00:51:51,389
Hey, Lee Hyeong Won!

711
00:51:52,547 --> 00:51:54,223
Where are you going?

712
00:51:56,305 --> 00:51:58,753
- What's it to you?
- I asked you a question.

713
00:51:58,753 --> 00:52:00,296
Get lost.

714
00:52:00,296 --> 00:52:01,645
Why?

715
00:52:01,645 --> 00:52:04,585
Are you giving up because of one lost match?

716
00:52:07,897 --> 00:52:09,382
Shut it.

717
00:52:09,382 --> 00:52:10,950
I'll still punch a girl.

718
00:52:10,950 --> 00:52:12,174
It's not over for you yet.

719
00:52:12,174 --> 00:52:13,782
There's a repechage, you know.

720
00:52:13,782 --> 00:52:15,761
You can secure a bronze medal if you're lucky.

721
00:52:15,761 --> 00:52:17,302
A bronze?

722
00:52:17,302 --> 00:52:19,069
What good is that?

723
00:52:19,069 --> 00:52:20,644
Who's going to acknowledge me for a 3rd place?

724
00:52:20,644 --> 00:52:22,224
Are you that out of touch?

725
00:52:22,224 --> 00:52:23,740
What's wrong with coming in 3rd place?

726
00:52:23,740 --> 00:52:25,266
It's better than running away
without even trying.

727
00:52:25,266 --> 00:52:27,940
Way cooler than the pathetic rat
you're acting like right now.

728
00:52:27,940 --> 00:52:30,219
It's not even worth the comparison, really.

729
00:52:31,184 --> 00:52:32,720
What did you just say?

730
00:52:35,294 --> 00:52:38,117
Hey, hey! The repechage, it's...

731
00:52:39,993 --> 00:52:41,927
- Uh, I...
- No way.

732
00:52:41,927 --> 00:52:43,587
We need to go see a doctor.

733
00:52:43,587 --> 00:52:44,831
Let's go.

734
00:52:44,831 --> 00:52:45,998
No, but...

735
00:52:45,998 --> 00:52:48,049
- But I...
- Ha Ru.

736
00:52:49,104 --> 00:52:50,683
Let's go to the hospital.

737
00:52:58,196 --> 00:52:59,590
Get back in there.

738
00:52:59,590 --> 00:53:02,575
You still have a chance at this.

739
00:53:02,575 --> 00:53:03,787
Choose.

740
00:53:03,787 --> 00:53:06,095
Do you want to be a judo player,

741
00:53:06,095 --> 00:53:08,159
or end up a miserable twat?

742
00:53:24,542 --> 00:53:26,341
[Baekyeon High School]

743
00:53:58,433 --> 00:53:59,950
I'm sorry.

744
00:54:01,406 --> 00:54:03,885
You told me not to get injured,

745
00:54:04,943 --> 00:54:07,143
but I couldn't even manage that.

746
00:54:08,417 --> 00:54:09,667
What are you on about?

747
00:54:09,667 --> 00:54:10,890
Don't tell me...

748
00:54:10,890 --> 00:54:13,250
You're conscious of me? That's so not you.

749
00:54:14,425 --> 00:54:16,625
I wanted to...

750
00:54:17,690 --> 00:54:20,235
protect your life as well, you know.

751
00:54:21,666 --> 00:54:23,312
Are you crying?

752
00:54:25,004 --> 00:54:29,337
How did you manage to memorize all those lines
as an actress with your empty noggin?

753
00:54:30,814 --> 00:54:33,598
- What?
- We came here for one reason.

754
00:54:33,598 --> 00:54:35,562
Don't tell me you forgot it already.

755
00:54:35,562 --> 00:54:36,848
Jung Woo Jae.

756
00:54:36,848 --> 00:54:40,576
Not my trials. Jung Woo Jae, got it?

757
00:54:40,576 --> 00:54:42,518
Idiot.

758
00:54:46,023 --> 00:54:48,872
We saw him make it into the team.

759
00:54:48,872 --> 00:54:50,668
Our work is over here.

760
00:54:51,779 --> 00:54:55,409
I'll save my own skin.
Don't make a big deal out of it.

761
00:54:57,042 --> 00:54:59,316
Well, now, let's go back!

762
00:55:01,057 --> 00:55:03,720
- But...
- What now?

763
00:55:03,720 --> 00:55:05,793
We don't know how to.

764
00:55:05,793 --> 00:55:07,224
Not yet.

765
00:55:07,224 --> 00:55:08,838
Damn, you're right.

766
00:55:17,860 --> 00:55:19,375
That didn't work.

767
00:55:20,461 --> 00:55:23,847
I guess just dropping it
isn't what triggers it.

768
00:55:25,199 --> 00:55:26,734
Well, let's try whatever we can.

769
00:55:26,734 --> 00:55:28,934
If it wants a fight, we'll give it a fight.

770
00:55:34,709 --> 00:55:36,833
Huh? What's up with the weather?

771
00:55:36,833 --> 00:55:38,767
Hey, are you alright?

772
00:55:38,767 --> 00:55:40,079
I'm fine.

773
00:55:46,683 --> 00:55:47,817
<i>Huh?</i>

774
00:55:47,817 --> 00:55:49,245
<i>What the...</i>

775
00:55:49,245 --> 00:55:51,672
<i>My alumna, Shin Bi Gyeong?</i>

776
00:55:51,672 --> 00:55:54,134
Hello, it's 2013.

777
00:55:54,134 --> 00:55:57,353
This is the after-party for
Yongwon University's Department of Film!

778
00:55:57,353 --> 00:55:59,717
Coming to you live!

779
00:55:59,717 --> 00:56:02,287
- Applaud!
<i>- 2013?</i>

780
00:56:02,287 --> 00:56:05,521
<i>Did the rain trigger another time leap?</i>

781
00:56:05,521 --> 00:56:10,043
Our alumni are getting blackout drunk
right now, as we speak!

782
00:56:10,043 --> 00:56:11,919
Let's see for ourselves.

783
00:56:11,919 --> 00:56:13,462
- Chug, chug, chug!
<i>- Ye Rang!</i>

784
00:56:13,462 --> 00:56:15,905
- Film is life!
<i>- Right, around this time, I assumed</i>

785
00:56:15,905 --> 00:56:17,836
<i>- she'd become an actress.</i>
- And life is a long take!

786
00:56:17,836 --> 00:56:21,752
<i>- And Jun Mo... He looks so young looking back.</i>
- Chug it, chug!

787
00:56:21,752 --> 00:56:24,796
<i>Han Soo Hyuk is... well, Han Soo Hyuk.</i>

788
00:56:24,796 --> 00:56:27,464
Let's hand it over to reporter Yoon Ha Na.

789
00:56:27,464 --> 00:56:30,234
Here you go, reporter Yoon Ha Na...

790
00:56:30,861 --> 00:56:34,824
Did you just call me Yoon Ha Na?

791
00:56:35,914 --> 00:56:38,012
Huh? It's me!

792
00:56:38,012 --> 00:56:39,987
It's Yoon Ha Na!

793
00:56:43,577 --> 00:56:45,325
But why 2013?

794
00:56:45,325 --> 00:56:48,367
Why not 2026? Why is it 2013?

795
00:56:48,367 --> 00:56:49,998
What's wrong, Ha Na?

796
00:56:49,998 --> 00:56:51,083
You alright, Ha Na?

797
00:56:51,083 --> 00:56:53,271
I'd be 21 in 2013...

798
00:56:53,271 --> 00:56:54,975
So, if he's 21...

799
00:56:54,975 --> 00:56:57,595
Woo Jae must be serving in the army.

800
00:57:00,721 --> 00:57:02,410
- Hey, where are you going?
- Yoon Ha Na!

801
00:57:02,410 --> 00:57:04,024
Where are you going?

802
00:57:05,971 --> 00:57:07,884
Why is this happening?

803
00:57:07,884 --> 00:57:10,195
What went wrong?

804
00:57:10,195 --> 00:57:13,622
[Beast]
Why won't he answer?

805
00:57:16,027 --> 00:57:17,521
Oh, my purse!

806
00:57:17,521 --> 00:57:18,631
Thief!

807
00:57:18,631 --> 00:57:21,263
- Move!
- It's a thief! A thief!

808
00:57:23,527 --> 00:57:24,740
Move!

809
00:57:24,740 --> 00:57:26,966
- He's a thief!
- Out of the way!

810
00:57:28,459 --> 00:57:30,142
You're not going anywhere!

811
00:57:31,686 --> 00:57:33,017
Piss off!

812
00:57:38,292 --> 00:57:39,828
Let go!

813
00:57:42,832 --> 00:57:43,833
Are you alright?

814
00:57:43,833 --> 00:57:45,506
Woo Jae!

815
00:57:51,877 --> 00:57:53,602
Are you hurt?

816
00:57:55,759 --> 00:57:57,366
You scum!

817
00:57:57,366 --> 00:57:58,866
Stay down!

818
00:58:10,879 --> 00:58:12,801
Oh, thank you.

819
00:58:25,236 --> 00:58:26,585
Ha Na.

820
00:58:26,585 --> 00:58:28,137
You sure you're okay?

821
00:58:28,137 --> 00:58:31,419
Oh, yeah, I'm totally fine.

822
00:58:32,050 --> 00:58:35,044
Are you sure you're okay?

823
00:58:35,044 --> 00:58:36,597
Of course I'm fine.

824
00:58:36,597 --> 00:58:38,276
I got your purse back, didn't I?

825
00:58:38,276 --> 00:58:40,574
No, I mean, you...

826
00:58:41,202 --> 00:58:42,313
Where do you live now?

827
00:58:42,313 --> 00:58:43,960
What about judo?

828
00:58:46,151 --> 00:58:48,888
Are you that drunk, Ha Na?

829
00:58:52,443 --> 00:58:53,966
I...

830
00:58:53,966 --> 00:58:55,838
I quit, remember?

831
00:58:56,578 --> 00:58:58,804
- Judo...
- What? Why?

832
00:58:58,804 --> 00:59:02,078
But you were first place in the national trial!
Why would you quit judo?

833
00:59:02,078 --> 00:59:03,578
I mean, why did you?

834
00:59:20,191 --> 00:59:21,798
Everyone's drinking a lot.

835
00:59:21,798 --> 00:59:23,704
I guess it's fair,
being the after-party of our campus festival.

836
00:59:23,704 --> 00:59:25,650
Our department seemed like
they wouldn't stop drinking, too.

837
00:59:25,650 --> 00:59:27,768
So I left after I got some dinner in me.

838
00:59:27,768 --> 00:59:29,493
- Your department?
- Yeah.

839
00:59:29,493 --> 00:59:32,742
By the way, we have a whopping
three new female students.

840
00:59:32,742 --> 00:59:35,250
Becoming a bodyguard was their childhood dream.

841
00:59:35,250 --> 00:59:36,738
How cool is that?

842
00:59:37,479 --> 00:59:39,108
Bodyguard?

843
00:59:41,969 --> 00:59:43,421
Yeah.

844
00:59:52,839 --> 00:59:54,130
[Beast]

845
00:59:54,845 --> 00:59:56,346
Just a moment.

846
00:59:56,346 --> 00:59:57,648
Okay.

847
00:59:59,346 --> 01:00:01,436
What took you so long?

848
01:00:01,436 --> 01:00:03,630
[Yoon's Raw Fish Restaurant]
<i>Yoon Ha Ru, where are you right now?</i>

849
01:00:04,595 --> 01:00:06,134
- Yoon Ha Na.
<i>- Yeah?</i>

850
01:00:06,134 --> 01:00:08,190
<i>Where the hell are you?</i>

851
01:00:08,190 --> 01:00:09,262
Haesol.

852
01:00:09,262 --> 01:00:10,368
Haesol?

853
01:00:10,368 --> 01:00:11,528
What are you doing there?

854
01:00:11,528 --> 01:00:13,403
Working part-time at our parents' restaurant.

855
01:00:13,403 --> 01:00:15,385
I'm not a judo player.

856
01:00:16,707 --> 01:00:20,399
I gave up... on judo.

857
01:00:22,039 --> 01:00:23,383
What?

858
01:00:57,863 --> 01:01:00,097
<i>Nothing's going as we expected.</i>

859
01:01:00,097 --> 01:01:04,630
<i>Everyone was worried about the two idiots
who knew nothing other than judo.</i>

860
01:01:04,630 --> 01:01:06,574
<i>How do I even do this?</i>

861
01:01:06,574 --> 01:01:07,813
<i>Chef.</i>

862
01:01:07,813 --> 01:01:10,517
<i>Why choose to be a bodyguard?</i>

863
01:01:10,517 --> 01:01:12,617
<i>I have someone I want to protect.</i>

864
01:01:12,617 --> 01:01:14,161
[That Summer, Us: Male Actor Audition]
<i>What if...</i>

865
01:01:14,161 --> 01:01:16,552
<i>that someone became the protector?</i>

866
01:01:16,552 --> 01:01:17,956
[We will protect Jung Woo Jae!]
<i>Ta-da!</i>

867
01:01:17,956 --> 01:01:19,330
<i>Woo Jae...</i>

868
01:01:19,330 --> 01:01:20,728
<i>I'm going to make him an actor.</i>

869
01:01:20,728 --> 01:01:23,318
<i>Physically adept, action-ready,
and a killer gaze. That's you!</i>

870
01:01:23,318 --> 01:01:25,742
<i>- Me?
- You'll be Jung Woo Jae, worldwide star!</i>

871
01:01:25,742 --> 01:01:30,277
<i>Turns out, it wasn't just the medal
that I wanted to take from you.</i>

872
01:01:30,277 --> 01:01:32,530
<i>If you can't put faith in yourself,</i>

873
01:01:32,530 --> 01:01:34,906
<i>put faith in me, who believes in you.</i>
